            },
            "body": "Reproduced on an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (SM120) on a tree without this fix: quantizing a column-sliced view against its contiguous copy leaves row 0 correct and every following row wrong, with no error raised - 1/2, 15/16 and 127/128 rows bad for (2, 512), (16, 1024) and (128, 4096) respectively, and the block scales differ too.\n\nThat's exactly the failure mode described, and calling `.contiguous()` right after the `reshape` is the right spot, since the reshape is what preserves the strided view in the first place. LGTM.\n",
